---
import { getCollection, render } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Annotation from '../components/Annotation.astro';
import PrincipleRefs from '../components/PrincipleRefs.astro';
import TierTag from '../components/TierTag.astro';
import { t, localePath } from '../lib/i18n.js';

const locale = 'en';

const all = await getCollection('cases', (entry) => entry.id.startsWith('en/'));
const sorted = [...all].sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
const slugOf = (entry) => entry.id.split('/').slice(1).join('/');

const drafted = await Promise.all(
  sorted
    .filter((entry) => entry.data.status === 'drafted')
    .map(async (entry) => ({ entry, slug: slugOf(entry), Content: (await render(entry)).Content }))
);
const toDraft = sorted
  .filter((entry) => entry.data.status === 'to-draft')
  .map((entry) => ({ entry, slug: slugOf(entry) }));

const SETTINGS = {
  fcc: 'Family child care',
  center: 'Center',
  'multi-site': 'Multi-site operator',
  intermediary: 'Intermediary',
};

const lastUpdated = sorted
  .map((entry) => entry.data.lastUpdated)
  .sort()
  .at(-1);

const description =
  'Short worked vignettes: the situation, what is at stake, what to do, and which principle governs.';
---

<BaseLayout title="Cases" description={description} locale={locale}>
  <PageHeader
    caption="Worked examples"
    title="Cases"
    lede="Nine situations a director actually meets, each one worked through to a decision she can make this week."
    locale={locale}
    lastUpdated={lastUpdated}
  />

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Almost every comparable framework is governance: who approves, what gets
    disclosed, how data is stored. Very little of it addresses the actual moment
    of use — the feature that switched itself on, the teacher at 6pm with an
    incident to write up, the family waiting for a screening result in a
    language nobody in the building speaks.
  </p>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    These are those moments. Every case has the same four parts: the situation,
    what is at stake, what to do, and which principle governs. They are written
    to be forwarded, so take any one of them on its own.
  </p>

  <nav class="govuk-!-margin-bottom-8" aria-labelledby="contents">
    <h2 class="govuk-heading-s" id="contents">{t(locale, 'label.onThisPage')}</h2>
    <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
      {drafted.map(({ entry, slug }) => (
        <li>
          <a class="govuk-link" href={`#${slug}`}>{entry.data.title}</a>
        </li>
      ))}
      <li><a class="govuk-link" href="#coming">Three more cases, coming</a></li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  {drafted.map(({ entry, slug, Content }) => (
    <section id={slug} class="govuk-!-margin-bottom-8">
      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m govuk-!-margin-bottom-2">{entry.data.title}</h2>

      <p class="govuk-body-s govuk-!-margin-bottom-4">
        {entry.data.tier !== undefined && (
          <span class="govuk-!-margin-right-3">
            <TierTag tier={entry.data.tier} locale={locale} />
          </span>
        )}
        {entry.data.settings.length > 0 && (
          <span>
            {t(locale, 'label.for')}:{' '}
            {entry.data.settings.map((s) => SETTINGS[s] ?? s).join(' · ')}
          </span>
        )}
      </p>

      <p class="govuk-body-l"><strong>{entry.data.situation}</strong></p>

      <Annotation label={t(locale, 'label.atStake')}>
        <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">{entry.data.atStake}</p>
      </Annotation>

      <Annotation label={t(locale, 'label.do')}>
        <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">{entry.data.whatToDo}</p>
      </Annotation>

      <div class="app-prose govuk-!-margin-bottom-4">
        <Content />
      </div>

      <PrincipleRefs
        ids={entry.data.governs}
        brightLines={entry.data.brightLines}
        locale={locale}
      />

      <hr class="govuk-section-break govuk-section-break--l govuk-section-break--visible" />
    </section>
  ))}

  <section id="coming">
    <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Three more cases, coming</h2>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      These three are named and are not written. Each one is here rather than
      quietly missing, because a director who meets one of these situations
      should know the site has not yet answered it.
    </p>

    <div class="govuk-inset-text">
      <dl class="govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">
        {toDraft.map(({ entry }) => (
          <>
            <dt class="govuk-body govuk-!-font-weight-bold govuk-!-margin-bottom-1">
              {entry.data.title}
            </dt>
            <dd class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-left-0 govuk-!-margin-bottom-4">
              {entry.data.situation}
            </dd>
          </>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </div>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      The library is meant to launch at eight or nine vignettes and then grow by
      roughly one a month. That growth is second-phase work: it depends on a
      convened body to stand behind the additions, and on the pilots and
      questions that body would bring with it. Until then the honest position is
      the one on this page — six worked through, three named and waiting.
    </p>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      If your situation is not here, the four pages behind these cases will
      usually get you to an answer:{' '}
      <a class="govuk-link" href={localePath(locale, '/bright-lines')}>the bright lines</a>,{' '}
      <a class="govuk-link" href={localePath(locale, '/principles')}>the principles</a>,{' '}
      <a class="govuk-link" href={localePath(locale, '/vendors')}>the vendor questions</a>{' '}
      and <a class="govuk-link" href={localePath(locale, '/start')}>the four-question intake</a>,
      which returns a tier.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
